WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.230
The Marvel Cinematic Universe has just gotten
a lot bigger, and a whole lot weirder in all

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.690
the best possible ways.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:11.280
Captain Marvel managed to burn through a whole
lot of story in a fun, fast-paced adventure

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.360
that sets up some exciting things for Avengers:
Endgame.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:18.279
But a movie jam-packed with this much awesome
stuff might be a little tough to follow from

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.280
start to finish.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.460
If you're looking to make sense of it all,
look no further: let's photon blast our way

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.669
through the plot of Captain Marvel and explain
just what the ending might mean.

00:00:27.669 --> 00:00:29.620
Strap in: major spoilers ahead.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.440
Captain Marvel begins on Hala, the homeworld
of the Kree.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.800
We're introduced to Vers a member of the planet's
group of Starforce warriors, and she's been

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.780
having nightmares.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.011
During training sessions with her mentor and
commander, Yon-Rogg, we learn that Vers is

00:00:43.011 --> 00:00:47.580
being trained to suppress her emotions, stop
questioning her mysterious past, and fight

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.300
without using her powers, which seem to consist
of having super-hot hands.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.920
But Vers sucks at emotion suppressing, and
she loves that whole hot-hand thing, so after

00:00:55.930 --> 00:01:00.240
a few too many photon blasts, she's sent to
be admonished by the Supreme Intelligence,

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.440
the artificial intelligence leader of the
Kree.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:07.070
The Supreme Intelligence appears differently
to everyone, and in Vers' case, it appears

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:08.280
as a mysterious woman.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.740
Good thing, too, because the Supreme Intelligence
is actually butt ugly and also supremely gross.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.260
"Okay, I may barf, but will someone tell me
what that thing is?"

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:23.520
Soon, Vers, Yon-Rogg, and the rest of Starforce
head off on a mission to rescue an undercover

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.380
Kree operative.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:29.220
But the whole thing turns out to be a Skrull
ambush and Vers is captured and interrogated

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:30.620
with a mind-scanning machine.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.840
That's where we conveniently catch more glimpses
of Vers' hidden memories, and the life she

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.860
used to live as an Air Force pilot on Earth.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:41.880
After mustering every ounce of willpower,
Vers escapes captivity, busts up a Skrull

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:46.670
ship, and zips down to Earth in an escape
pod, followed by a squad of Skrull warriors,

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.180
led by a guy named Talos.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:53.220
Their mission: find a hidden lightspeed engine
developed by scientist Doctor Wendy Lawson.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:57.540
After crash-landing into a Blockbuster video,
Vers finds herself stuck on Earth.

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:01.740
So she places a long-distance call to her
Starforce buddies to tell them she's going

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.820
after the Skrulls.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:07.860
It isn't long before Vers encounters the local
law enforcement and the feds in the form of

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.540
Nick Fury, Agent of SHIELD.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:14.400
Just as Fury and his partner, Agent Phil Coulson,
are about to arrest her for the crime of busting

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.440
holes into video stores, she's attacked by
a Skrull sniper and gives chase.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:23.279
Fury and Coulson likewise chase the chaser,
and we soon discover that the guy riding shotgun

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.740
with Fury isn't Coulson at all...but a Skrull
now dead who took his place.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.959
Once the chase ends, Vers seeks answers from
her recently unlocked memories, while Fury

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.660
joins her in her quest to discover the location
of Doctor Lawson's engine.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.060
Meanwhile, SHIELD has been infiltrated with
at least one Skrull operative — Talos — who's

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.700
impersonating Fury's boss, Agent Keller.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.420
Fury and Vers head to Project Pegasus to learn
about Lawson's work.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:51.660
There they encounter Lawson's cat named Goose
a photo of Vers as a human fighter pilot,

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:53.340
and also those darned Skrulls.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:58.510
A fight ensues, and Vers and Fury steal an
experimental flight craft and head to Louisiana,

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:02.739
where they hope to get more answers about
Vers' former life from Maria Rambeau, who

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:06.120
was the last person to see Lawson — and
Vers — alive on Earth.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.219
The reunion with Rambeau and her daughter
Monica is bittersweet, as Vers learns her

00:03:10.219 --> 00:03:15.329
true identity of Carol Danvers, a test pilot
who was presumed dead six years ago after

00:03:15.329 --> 00:03:17.680
a flight with Lawson's special project went
wrong.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:21.999
But even as Rambeau fills in the gaps about
her life as Danvers, she's unable to remember

00:03:21.999 --> 00:03:26.590
as much about her past as she'd like she can
only retain glimpses of her memories, and

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:30.840
many of them are memories of various failures,
like crashing a go-kart or falling from the

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.340
ropes course during her time in basic training.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:37.700
While gathering more memories, however, the
house is infiltrated by Talos and another

00:03:37.709 --> 00:03:42.829
Skrull but this time, instead of threatening
Danvers and her friends, Talos offers a truce,

00:03:42.829 --> 00:03:44.760
and an audio recording of Danvers' "death."

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:49.480
Here's were we learn the truth: Danvers and
Lawson were shot down by a Kree spacecraft,

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.240
piloted by none other than Yon-Rogg.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:56.419
Yon-Rogg kills Lawson a secret Kree operative
named Mar-Vell who'd gone rogue, and whose

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:00.020
experimental project was meant to peacefully
end the Kree-Skrull war.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:04.380
Danvers realizes she's been fighting for the
wrong side, and the Kree had erased her memories

00:04:04.389 --> 00:04:08.730
and abducted her from Earth after she gained
her powers, a side-effect of her decision

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:13.120
to blow up the engine of Lawson's experimental
craft to keep it out of Yon-Rogg's hands.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:17.280
Danvers and the Skrulls strike a truce, and
they fly off to find Mar-Vell's power source

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.000
before the Kree can snatch it away.

00:04:19.329 --> 00:04:24.420
Once aboard Mar-Vell's orbiting space-lab,
Danvers, Fury, Rambeau, Talos, and Goose find

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.800
her power source: the Tesseract, also known
as the Space Stone.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:32.419
But that isn't the only secret the lab holds,
as Talos's family and a bunch of other Skrull

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:35.820
refugees are aboard, having lived there for
the last six years.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.380
The reunion is interrupted by Yon-Rogg and
the rest of Starforce.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.760
Danvers is captured and plugged into the Supreme
Intelligence, who taunts Danvers about her

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.040
rediscovered humanity saying that being human
sucks.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:48.200
Wrong move!

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:52.440
Danvers overcomes the Supreme Intelligence,
and breaks free of the Kree's suppression

00:04:52.449 --> 00:04:53.639
of her superpowers.

00:04:53.639 --> 00:04:58.490
Meanwhile, Fury and Talos beat up some Kree
warriors with relative ease when you think

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.700
about the alleged Kree training an all…
and make their escape from the lab.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:06.560
In the process, Goose reveals himself to be
not a cat, but rather a Flerken, an alien

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:11.080
sight-gag able to swallow magical Macguffins
with the help of CGI tentacles.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:15.400
The Tesseract is safe within his belly, and
the gang leaves the lab to head back to Earth.

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:20.560
Danvers, now more powerful than ever, beats
up Starforce, blasts Yon-Rogg, and explodes

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.120
some super-bombs deployed by Ronan the Accuser.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:28.020
The Kree leave Earth, and Danvers does likewise
to help the Skrull refugees find a new home

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.340
— and end the Kree-Skrull war for good.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:34.440
She leaves Fury a souped up pager to be used
only for emergencies.

00:05:34.449 --> 00:05:38.629
Finally, in the mid-credits scene, we see
her return to Earth 20 years later, where

00:05:38.629 --> 00:05:41.380
the activated pager sits in Avengers headquarters.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.980
So, now that we know what happens in the movie,
what's it all mean?

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:48.900
During the beginning of the film, Yon-Rogg
tells Danvers she needs to dampen her emotions

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.860
and control herself and her powers.

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:54.910
He tells her she needs to be the best version
of herself — but the best version by his

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:55.400
standards.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.440
As we see memories of her past, we see others
telling Danvers what she must do — or what

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.280
she can't do.

00:06:00.449 --> 00:06:02.280
She needs to slow down her go-kart.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.800
She needs to quit basic training.

00:06:04.009 --> 00:06:06.720
She needs to accept that flying is for men,
not women.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:10.500
And finally, during her last confrontation
with the Supreme Intelligence, she needs to

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:14.520
accept that without the Kree, she's only human,
and that's not enough to succeed.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:17.700
Naturally, Danvers realizes that everyone's
been dead wrong.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.320
Being a woman never stopped her from being
a kick-ass pilot, while being an emotional

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.389
human helped her beat all of Starforce single-handedly.

00:06:24.389 --> 00:06:28.140
If you didn't catch the intended theme of
the film by that point, No Doubt's "I'm Just

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:32.169
a Girl" playing during the fight scene with
Starforce might have driven the point of the

00:06:32.169 --> 00:06:32.680
movie home.

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:37.419
And by finally letting loose and embracing
her humanity emotions and all Danvers discovers

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:40.620
she can literally fly, no plane or spaceship
required.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:44.310
In short, the ending of the movie proves that
you shouldn't let anyone tell you that you

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:48.750
need to fight against your nature to be your
best self your best self might be exactly

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.280
who you already were all along.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:55.419
With six Infinity Stones floating around the
edges of 21 different movies, no one would

00:06:55.419 --> 00:06:58.270
blame you for having a hard time keeping track
of all of them.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:02.430
As such, you probably weren't the only one
to gasp in recognition and confusion when

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:05.680
the Tesseract showed up in Mar-Vell's secret
floating space lab.

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:09.990
The last time we saw that thing, it was sitting
pretty on Thanos's Infinity Gauntlet, having

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:13.719
been liberated from Loki's possession at the
beginning of Avengers: Infinity War.

00:07:13.719 --> 00:07:17.770
And before that, it played important roles
in the first Captain America and Avengers

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:18.770
movies.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:22.850
So how'd it end up in Mar-Vell's possession...only
to later be swallowed and coughed up by an

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:23.940
alien space cat?

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:27.770
For those who don't recall, the Tesseract
zapped Red Skull into space at the end of

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:29.759
Captain America: The First Avenger.

00:07:29.759 --> 00:07:33.740
Later, Howard Stark recovered the Tesseract
on the bottom of the ocean while searching

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:38.069
for the lost Steve Rogers, and eventually
it was given to SHIELD for safekeeping.

00:07:38.069 --> 00:07:42.409
The next time the Tesseract appears is in
the Avengers film, when Loki breaks into SHIELD

00:07:42.409 --> 00:07:44.169
headquarters to steal it.

00:07:44.169 --> 00:07:48.469
Its appearance in Captain Marvel fills in
some blanks in terms of the Tesseract's importance

00:07:48.469 --> 00:07:50.419
in shaping the MCU's future.

00:07:50.419 --> 00:07:54.379
However, it does raise some questions: No
one at SHIELD wondered where the glowing blue

00:07:54.379 --> 00:07:56.319
space-cube had disappeared to?

00:07:56.319 --> 00:08:00.569
What kind of paperwork did Doctor Lawson had
to fill out in order to gain access to the

00:08:00.569 --> 00:08:01.560
Tesseract for her experiments?

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.560
"Get ready for a large file transfer."

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:04.280
"How large?"

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:12.600
There are several cool ways Captain Marvel
establishes itself within the MCU's greater

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:13.220
continuity.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:17.060
The movie does a pretty good job of ensuring
that little if anything happening in this

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:20.320
film contradicts any of the movies that take
place after it.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:24.260
That's a feat many prequels attempt and at
which only a few really succeed.

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:29.620
For instance, we now know how Fury lost his
eye, from a nasty scratch by the flerken Cat.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:34.580
The scratch solves a longtime MCU mystery,
while also helping us understand how and why

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:38.760
Fury is able to cope with all the weirdness
of super-people without breaking a sweat.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:43.390
He lost his eye to an alien tentacle-cat while
escaping a bunch of murderous Kree soldiers.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.060
He can handle a few Norse gods.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.640
We also learn that the name for the Avengers
Initiative was inspired by Carol Danvers,

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:51.740
whose call-sign as a pilot was "Avenger."

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:56.260
Fury's super-pager, which he used to contact
Captain Marvel at the end of Avengers: Infinity

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:57.740
War, gets an origin story, too.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:02.720
In all, Danvers and her quest had a definitive
impact on Fury personally and the larger unfolding

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:03.730
of the MCU.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:08.310
And yet, the pager still raises at least one
huge question about what defines an "emergency"

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:09.650
to Nick Fury.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:14.120
In Avengers, for instance, a wormhole opened
over Manhattan and pooped out a bunch of alien

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:14.620
invaders.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:19.780
The second Avengers movie featured a super-evil
robot attempting a world takeover and an entire

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.340
city floating in the sky.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:22.760
Those weren't emergencies?

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:27.560
MCU boss Kevin Feige offered an answer to
that question the during the weekend of Captain

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:28.280
Marvel's release.

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:32.700
When asked by SlashFilm why Fury never hit
the pager during those other crises, Feige

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:33.200
answered:

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:35.280
"How do you know he never hit it?

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:37.190
How do we know he never pushed it before?

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.760
We’ve never seen him push it before.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.140
That doesn’t mean he never did."

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:45.140
The mid-credits scene in Captain Marvel gives
us a preview of Avengers: Endgame.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:49.860
Danvers swoops into Avengers HQ in response
to Fury's pager, which has been sending its

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:52.280
signal into space since Infinity War's end.

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:56.350
It confirms that Captain Marvel will have
a significant role in the restoration of half

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:57.880
the universe's population.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.560
Good thing she wasn't dusted, too!

00:09:59.730 --> 00:10:03.740
Beyond that, it's likely we'll get more adventures
with Captain Marvel on Earth once Endgame's

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:04.540
credits roll.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:08.820
While she's unlocked most, if not all of her
pre-Kree memories, she still hasn't spent

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.020
time actually reacclimating to life on her
homeworld.

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:16.200
The events of Captain Marvel take place in
1995, six years after her abduction.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:20.520
Now she's returned home after another twenty
years, though she still looks as young as

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.520
ever, thanks to her superpowered Kree blood.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:26.960
And just like Captain America before her,
Danvers is out of her own time, and we'll

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:31.520
probably see her struggling to reconnect after
over a quarter century away from home.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:35.780
Additionally, Monica Rambeau, Maria's daughter,
probably has a role to play, based on the

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.580
character's history from the comics.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:43.360
In 1982, she made her debut as a hero named
Captain Marvel, only her origin story didn't

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:46.580
really have anything to do with Danvers, Mar-Vell,
or the Kree.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:51.340
In the MCU, though, she'll be 20 years older...and
probably ready to either join Captain Marvel

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:55.440
on her next adventure, or become her own Captain
Marvel further down the line.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:58.280
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:02.380
Plus, even more Looper videos about the Marvel
Cinematic Universe are coming soon.

